{"author_association":"OWNER","body":"## Independent PM final review — G5 APPROVED WITH LIMITATIONS (2026-11-01)\n\n**Review target:** PR #20, exact HEAD `ec7ab8c0fe097004eb4d37018be898c68f41364b`, base `initial-idea` at `0f45fa06c235658da48d3d41a9091c06580bfe27`.\n\n**Independent PM verdict: APPROVE G5 delivery acceptance for M7-04 and M7-05, with the existing scientific and environment-verification limitations. Finding G5-F01 is RESOLVED. PR #20 is accepted for integration at this reviewed HEAD.**\n\n**Crucial boundary: NO RELEASE / NO PUBLICATION AUTHORIZED.** G5 approval is acceptance of the documentation/handover and the explicit no-release disposition. It neither authorizes nor implies any public model/data/ROM distribution, third-party access, external upload, deployment, GitHub Release, or publication. A future release requires a separate explicit Project Owner decision and artifact-specific rights/privacy/integrity/scientific-claims review.\n\n### Independent findings\n\n1. **G5-F01 provenance correction — ACCEPTED.** Direct comparison with `.agents/evidence/M3-final-closure-record-20261021.json`, `M3-acceptance-20261021.md`, `M3-corrective-reproducibility-r4-r5-20261021.json`, and `M3-corrective-teacher-manifest-r2-20261021.json` confirms:\n   - Accepted final M3 r6/r7 release `f10a679deddf06f3e1e3c39cf58db4e21176629c26c09034a271bf278189e890` correctly pairs with manifest `be1e1f9316fac01be893774cfe09a313de193fbd1a12ab2d219ff5c041104a12`; accepted teacher-r1 `58febd814bb6bdd6fa67b990a1e4906ada14c31fafa265829fb49b7d3c203272` binds to that pair.\n   - Historical corrective M3 r4/r5 release `7b51ec3761ad28aa7a2882691b3c314d35115ab339769251ff2556e706a5b1d9` correctly pairs with manifest `77e217423e187278c584b8f566a846fd606bddaadad19179b7bef63959bd5abe`; historical teacher-r2 `ba4a109064e05ac5d0ec966892745f04fefea014faa8287d977e94fc5f685826` binds to that historical generation.\n   - `RELEASE_DISPOSITION.md` and `HANDOVER.md` now distinguish the generations without modifying accepted artifact source records. The new tests check relationships from structured evidence; their three provenance checks demonstrably failed against the original incorrect inventory before passing after correction.\n2. **M7-04 — ACCEPTED.** The four required report/model-card/user-guide/handover deliverables were independently accepted in the prior PM decision on [PR #19](https://github.com/dodaonam/atari-videochess-rl/pull/19#issuecomment-6553580590). This review verifies the current M7-005 delivery updates and G5-F01 provenance references remain consistent.\n3. **M7-05 — ACCEPTED as NO RELEASE.** The owner instruction and decision records (`M7-AUTH-20261101-M7-005-NO-RELEASE`, `M7-REL-DISP-20261101-NO-RELEASE`) support an explicit no-release/no-publication disposition, with restricted artifact categories, rights limitations, future-review conditions and no implied redistribution permission.\n4. **Scientific boundaries — PRESERVED.** M7 retains 90 started/reset-observed attempts, 60 terminal White losses, 30 incomplete, zero wins/draws, limited paired terminal evidence (9/30 Warm/Scratch cells), no demonstrated RL superiority/equivalence/generalization, no calibrated Elo, and unresolved O-02/O-06, RSK-014, and PM6-F06. M4/M5/M6 v1/M6 v2/M7 evidence remains separate; no accepted science was amended.\n5. **Verification — ACCEPTED WITH ENVIRONMENT QUALIFICATION.** Retained clean-clone focused suite: 86 PASS. Full unfiltered clean-clone suite: 513 tests, **one failure** because the Stockfish UCI executable is unavailable, three skips; this is **not** a full-suite pass. Precisely excluding that one environment-dependent readiness test: 512 tests, three skips, zero failures/errors. Three skipped private-artifact tests and the expected `ARTIFACT_MANIFEST_REQUIRED` warning remain disclosed. Comparing `0d3ee8221698f52bf2c7658657e505900ab5485d` to the final HEAD shows no subsequent application or test-source changes; subsequent commits only add/update documentation, evidence/logs, and checkpoint metadata. [GitHub Repository preflight run 41297779574](https://github.com/dodaonam/atari-videochess-rl/actions/runs/41297779574) succeeded at the **exact reviewed HEAD**. Its `context` job is not the full Python suite.\n6. **Governance / safety — ACCEPTED.** At review, M7-001–005 are engineering DONE, G4 remains approved with scientific limitations, and the PR's pre-decision canonical state appropriately still lists G5 pending. The changed-file inventory shows governance, docs, tests, sanitized logs/evidence/checkpoint metadata, without accepted experiment payload/config/checkpoint/manifest changes. No permission to release is created.\n\n### Decision and closeout instructions\n\n- **G5: APPROVED WITH SCIENTIFIC, ENVIRONMENT-VERIFICATION, AND NO-RELEASE LIMITATIONS for M7-04/M7-05 at the exact HEAD above.**\n- **G5-F01: CLOSED / RESOLVED.**\n- **PR #20: APPROVED FOR INTEGRATION at this reviewed HEAD; currently unmerged.** No merge is performed by this review comment. A new code-bearing commit or material change requires renewed review.\n- After authorized integration, record this actual PM decision in a **separate, evidence-linked canonical governance closeout** as appropriate to the repository's previous G4 closeout pattern. Do not mark the pre-merge PR as already integrated and do not self-author any PM decision. Link this comment as the authoritative decision evidence.\n- **NO RELEASE / NO PUBLICATION AUTHORIZED** remains binding after any G5 or merge-state update. No release, distribution, upload, or deployment may follow automatically.\n\nThis is the independent PM's explicit G5 decision; it is not an executor self-approval and is not a Project Owner permission to publish.","created_at":"2026-11-01T10:39:28Z","html_url":"https://github.com/dodaonam/atari-videochess-rl/pull/20#issuecomment-6556836388","id":6556836388,"updated_at":"2026-11-01T10:39:28Z","user":"dodaonam"}
